---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { DIGUP_UI, SITE } from '../lib/site';
---
<Layout
  title="DigUp Guide — On-Device Multimodal Semantic File Search"
  description="Independent coverage of DigUp (ARahim3/DigUp) — local EmbeddingGemma 2 search for photos, PDFs, audio, video, and code on Mac, Windows, and Linux. Install links to GitHub Releases."
  canonicalPath="/"
  lang="en"
  ogImage={DIGUP_UI.hero.src}
>
  <main>
    <section class="hero wrap">
      <div class="hero-split">
        <div class="hero-copy">
          <span class="badge">On-device · Multimodal</span>
          <h1>Describe it. Dig it up on your machine.</h1>
          <ul class="job-steps" aria-label="How DigUp works">
            <li><span class="n">1</span> Describe</li>
            <li class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</li>
            <li><span class="n">2</span> Hit content</li>
            <li class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</li>
            <li><span class="n">3</span> Open at page / time / line</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="lede">
            DigUp is open-source, on-device multimodal semantic file search. Natural language finds what’s <em>inside</em> photos, PDFs, docs, audio, and video (optional code) — private folder indexing, not a cloud drive, not a launcher, not another AI chat. This site is independent coverage; downloads only from GitHub Releases.
          </p>
          <div class="hero-actions">
            <a class="cta" href={SITE.upstreamReleases} rel="noopener noreferrer">Download on GitHub Releases</a>
            <a class="cta-secondary" href="/install-mac/">Mac install guide</a>
          </div>
          <p class="hero-brew">
            Mac Homebrew: <code>{SITE.brewCask}</code>
          </p>
        </div>

        <figure class="shot-panel">
          <span class="shot-label">Real DigUp UI · Mac</span>
          <img
            src={DIGUP_UI.hero.src}
            width="1200"
            height="800"
            alt={DIGUP_UI.hero.altEn}
            loading="eager"
            decoding="async"
          />
          <figcaption class="shot-caption">{DIGUP_UI.sourceNoteEn} Query shown: “zebra in a video” → open at 0:42.</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="wrap section-head">
      <p class="section-label">Real UI</p>
      <h2>Search box → result list → open to page / timestamp</h2>
      <p class="muted">Stills from the official DigUp <code>docs/demo.gif</code> (ARahim3/DigUp). Compressed WebP for this guide.</p>
      <div class="shot-gallery">
        <figure class="shot-panel">
          <span class="shot-label">Windows · PDF page</span>
          <img src={DIGUP_UI.pdf.src} width="1200" height="800" alt={DIGUP_UI.pdf.altEn} loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          <figcaption>“the clause about pets in the lease” → Lease PDF <strong>p. 4</strong>.</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="shot-panel">
          <span class="shot-label">Mac · Audio time</span>
          <img src={DIGUP_UI.audio.src} width="1200" height="800" alt={DIGUP_UI.audio.altEn} loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          <figcaption>“where they talk about sleep” → open near <strong>7:55</strong>.</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="shot-panel">
          <span class="shot-label">Windows · Result list</span>
          <img src={DIGUP_UI.multimodal.src} width="1200" height="800" alt={DIGUP_UI.multimodal.altEn} loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          <figcaption>“a dog on the beach” — images, video, audio, and a PDF hit in one list.</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="shot-panel">
          <span class="shot-label">Linux · Code</span>
          <img src={DIGUP_UI.code.src} width="1200" height="800" alt={DIGUP_UI.code.altEn} loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          <figcaption><code>code:</code> retry with backoff — open to the matching line.</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
      <aside class="demo-panel secondary" aria-label="Abstract flow mock (secondary)">
        <span class="demo-label">Abstract mock (support only)</span>
        <div class="demo-search" role="img" aria-label="Example search query">
          <span class="q-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span class="query">the clause about pets in the lease<span class="cursor" aria-hidden="true"></span></span>
        </div>
        <div class="demo-results">
          <div class="demo-hit active">
            <div class="demo-thumb pdf" aria-hidden="true"><span>PDF</span><span>p.12</span></div>
            <div class="meta">
              <h3>Lease_2024.pdf</h3>
              <p>…pets allowed with written notice…</p>
            </div>
            <span class="loc">→ page 12</span>
          </div>
          <div class="demo-hit">
            <div class="demo-thumb vid" aria-hidden="true"></div>
            <div class="meta">
              <h3>safari_clip.mp4</h3>
              <p>Match: “zebra crossing the road”</p>
            </div>
            <span class="loc">→ 02:14</span>
          </div>
          <div class="demo-hit">
            <div class="demo-thumb img" aria-hidden="true">IMG</div>
            <div class="meta">
              <h3>IMG_4821.heic</h3>
              <p>Dog on the beach at sunset</p>
            </div>
            <span class="loc">→ open</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="demo-caption">CSS wireframe of the same job — secondary to the real screenshots above.</p>
      </aside>
    </section>

    <section class="wrap section-head">
      <p class="section-label">How you use it</p>
      <h2>Three searches that show the job</h2>
      <p class="muted">Same idea every time: say what you remember about the contents; DigUp jumps to the place inside the file.</p>
      <div class="scenarios">
        <article class="scenario">
          <span class="mod-pill text">PDF / docs</span>
          <p class="query-line">the clause about pets in the lease</p>
          <ul class="flow">
            <li><span class="k">Find</span> <span>Meaning match in a long PDF</span></li>
            <li><span class="k">Open</span> <span><strong>Page 4</strong> in your PDF viewer</span></li>
          </ul>
        </article>
        <article class="scenario">
          <span class="mod-pill video">Video</span>
          <p class="query-line">zebra in a video</p>
          <ul class="flow">
            <li><span class="k">Find</span> <span>Frame + soundtrack window</span></li>
            <li><span class="k">Open</span> <span>Clip at <strong>0:42</strong></span></li>
          </ul>
        </article>
        <article class="scenario">
          <span class="mod-pill audio">Audio</span>
          <p class="query-line">where they talk about sleep</p>
          <ul class="flow">
            <li><span class="k">Find</span> <span>~30s audio window by meaning</span></li>
            <li><span class="k">Open</span> <span>Podcast at that <strong>minute</strong></span></li>
          </ul>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="wrap section-head">
      <p class="section-label">What you search</p>
      <h2>Modality matrix — content, not platforms</h2>
      <p class="muted">Scannable at a glance: one shared embedding space across file types you choose to index. Platforms are install details below.</p>
      <div class="modality-grid">
        <div class="modality image">
          <div class="icon" aria-hidden="true">▣</div>
          <h3>Images</h3>
          <p>Photos &amp; screenshots by what’s shown</p>
        </div>
        <div class="modality text">
          <div class="icon" aria-hidden="true">¶</div>
          <h3>PDFs / docs</h3>
          <p>Pages &amp; passages → open to page</p>
        </div>
        <div class="modality audio">
          <div class="icon" aria-hidden="true">♫</div>
          <h3>Audio</h3>
          <p>Meaning in ~30s windows → timestamp</p>
        </div>
        <div class="modality video">
          <div class="icon" aria-hidden="true">▶</div>
          <h3>Video</h3>
          <p>Frames + sound → moment</p>
        </div>
        <div class="modality code">
          <div class="icon" aria-hidden="true">&lbrace;&rbrace;</div>
          <h3>Code</h3>
          <p>Optional <code>code:</code> → line in editor</p>
        </div>
        <div class="modality local">
          <div class="icon" aria-hidden="true">⌂</div>
          <h3>On-device</h3>
          <p>Folders you pick · no cloud index</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="wrap section-head">
      <p class="section-label">vs Spotlight</p>
      <h2>Different job: names vs what’s inside</h2>
      <div class="vs-strip">
        <div class="vs-col">
          <h3>Spotlight</h3>
          <p>Apps, filenames, metadata, and a lot of plaintext. Best for “open X” and “find file named Y.”</p>
        </div>
        <div class="vs-mid" aria-hidden="true">vs</div>
        <div class="vs-col digup">
          <h3>DigUp</h3>
          <p><strong>Content dimension:</strong> describe a photo, PDF page, recording, or video moment — open to that location. Local EmbeddingGemma 2.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p><a href="/vs-spotlight/">Full DigUp vs Spotlight comparison →</a></p>
    </section>

    <section class="wrap section-head">
      <p class="section-label">Install</p>
      <h2>Verify on GitHub before install</h2>
      <p class="muted">Numbers checked via GitHub API on 2026-10-15: ~3,716 stars · forks 252 · MIT. Platforms are secondary to the search job above.</p>
      <div class="platform-grid">
        <div class="platform">
          <h3>macOS</h3>
          <p class="ver">0.6.1 stable</p>
          <p class="muted">Apple Silicon · macOS 14+</p>
          <p><a href="/install-mac/">Install on Mac →</a></p>
        </div>
        <div class="platform">
          <h3>Windows</h3>
          <p class="ver beta">0.7.0-beta.1</p>
          <p class="muted">64-bit Win 10/11 · unsigned installer</p>
          <p><a href="/install-windows/">Install on Windows →</a></p>
        </div>
        <div class="platform">
          <h3>Linux</h3>
          <p class="ver beta">0.7.0-beta.1</p>
          <p class="muted">.deb · AppImage · amd64</p>
          <p><a href="/install-linux/">Install on Linux →</a></p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="wrap section-head">
      <p class="section-label">Guides</p>
      <h2>Guides on this site</h2>
      <div class="cards">
        <a class="card" href="/what-is-digup/">
          <span class="tag">Overview</span>
          <h3>What is DigUp?</h3>
          <p>Modalities, how indexing works, and OS requirements in one place.</p>
        </a>
        <a class="card" href="/install-mac/">
          <span class="tag">Install</span>
          <h3>Install on Mac</h3>
          <p>Homebrew cask or DMG, first-run ~865 MB model, ⇧⌘Space.</p>
        </a>
        <a class="card" href="/install-windows/">
          <span class="tag">Beta</span>
          <h3>Install on Windows</h3>
          <p>x64 setup from Releases, SmartScreen “Run anyway,” GPU notes.</p>
        </a>
        <a class="card" href="/install-linux/">
          <span class="tag">Beta</span>
          <h3>Install on Linux</h3>
          <p>.deb for Ubuntu/Debian/Mint, AppImage elsewhere, Wayland shortcuts.</p>
        </a>
        <a class="card" href="/vs-spotlight/">
          <span class="tag">Compare</span>
          <h3>DigUp vs Spotlight</h3>
          <p>Filename/metadata vs meaning — when to use both on Mac.</p>
        </a>
        <a class="card" href="/embeddinggemma-2/">
          <span class="tag">Model</span>
          <h3>EmbeddingGemma 2</h3>
          <p>How DigUp runs Google’s model locally via llama.cpp (~865 MB).</p>
        </a>
        <a class="card" href="/faq/">
          <span class="tag">Support</span>
          <h3>FAQ</h3>
          <p>Privacy, Intel Mac, indexing time, code search, beta meaning.</p>
        </a>
        <a class="card" href="/zh/">
          <span class="tag">中文</span>
          <h3>中文指南</h3>
          <p>首页与安装 / 对比 / FAQ 中文版（/zh/）。</p>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="wrap" style="margin-top:0.5rem;">
      <p class="section-label">Audience</p>
      <h2 style="margin-top:0;">Who this site is for</h2>
      <ul class="checklist">
        <li>People who searched for <strong>DigUp Mac</strong>, brew install, or Windows/Linux beta setup and want a scannable checklist.</li>
        <li>Anyone comparing DigUp to Spotlight on the <strong>content</strong> dimension — photos, PDF pages, audio/video moments — not filenames alone.</li>
        <li>Readers who want independent English / Chinese how-tos with outbound links — not another binary mirror or AI chat wrapper.</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="cta-bar">
        <a class="cta" href={SITE.upstreamReleases} rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub Releases</a>
        <a class="cta-secondary" href="/what-is-digup/">Start with What is DigUp</a>
        <a class="cta-secondary" href="/zh/">中文首页</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>
